# PhoneLight server configuration: copy to .env in the app directory
# (install.sh does this for you). .env is gitignored and never committed.
# systemd loads it via EnvironmentFile=. Restart after editing:
#   sudo systemctl restart phonelight
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, no spaces around '='. Lines starting with
# # are comments. No inline comments and no $VAR expansion.
#
# Show settings (universe, start address, fixtures, 8/16-bit, master, loss
# hold/fade, data retention) are NOT here: set them on the admin Settings page.

# ── Web server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Guests open http://<this server>:APP_PORT/ ; the admin is at /admin.
APP_PORT=5420
# Open sockets the one gevent worker accepts (phones + admin pages + spare).
#MAX_CONNECTIONS=4000
# 1 = log every HTTP request to the journal.
#ACCESS_LOG=1
# Behind the gateway (gateway/README.md): the gateway's address as this server
# sees it (cyclorama's tunnel address), comma-separated IPs / networks. Only
# requests FROM that address have X-Forwarded-For / -Proto believed (the
# guest's real IP); anyone else's are ignored. Requests through the gateway
# never get the admin. The gateway installer prints the value to use.
# (Old value 1 still works but believes the header from anyone: replace it.)
#TRUST_PROXY=10.201.4.9

# ── Admin access ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is no admin sign-in yet. Limit /admin to these IPs / networks
# (comma-separated); guests on other addresses get 403 there. Empty = anyone
# on the network (requests through the gateway are always refused).
# Checked against the real connecting address, never a forwarded one.
#ADMIN_ALLOW=192.168.10.0/24,127.0.0.1
# The admin answers only when opened by IP address or localhost (a web page
# can't point another name at it: DNS rebinding). Extra names, comma-separated:
#ADMIN_HOSTS=glow-server.local

# ── sACN in ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unicast only (no multicast join). Bind to one interface's IP to listen on
# that network only; 0.0.0.0 = every interface.
#SACN_BIND=0.0.0.0
#SACN_PORT=5568
# sACN has no password: anyone who can send UDP here drives the phones. Accept
# it only from the console(s) (IPs / networks, comma-separated); empty = anyone.
#SACN_ALLOW=192.168.10.20

# ── Public URL abuse ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Phone sockets one address may hold (0 = no limit), so one machine can't
# take every connection. A venue Wi-Fi shows as ONE address (NAT): list such
# addresses in MAX_PER_IP_EXEMPT (IPs / networks, comma-separated).
#MAX_PER_IP=20
#MAX_PER_IP_EXEMPT=

# ── Database (SQLite for the trial; PostgreSQL later) ────────────────────────
# Relative paths are inside the app directory.
#DB_PATH=data/phonelight.db
